.* Multi Poker Help
:userdoc.

:h1 res=001.General Help
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Multi Poker is a five card draw video poker game, like the machines found in casinos. Unlike the machines, it also tells you the best play. Choose a topic&colon.
:p.
:ul compact.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=002.Playing a hand:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=003.The games:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=004.Advice and odds:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=005.Menus and keys:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=006.About Multi Poker and license:elink.
:eul.
:p.

:h1 res=002.Playing a hand
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Choose :hp2.Game - New Game:ehp2. to get $25 in the bank. Wager $1 to $5 with the :hp2.Bet:ehp2. button (or the + key); each press adds a dollar. :hp2.Bet Five:ehp2. (space bar) wagers $5 at once. A $5 wager deals the cards automatically, since no more money can be wagered on a hand.
:p.
The first five cards are dealt and the value of the hand is shown above the cards. At first all the cards are marked :hp2.Discard:ehp2.. Press the :hp2.Keep/Discard:ehp2. button under a card (keys F5 to F9, or 1 to 5) to keep it. Press :hp2.Deal:ehp2. (key D) to replace the discarded cards. The final hand is paid according to the payout table; the column of your wager and the row of your hand are highlighted.
:p.
When the bank is empty choose Game - New Game for another $25. The game cannot be changed in the middle of a hand.

:h1 res=003.The games
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
The games are the libraries in the games folder next to MPoker.exe. Each one appears in :hp2.Game - Select:ehp2.. The game you played last is selected when the program starts.
:ul.
:li.:hp2.Jacks or Better:ehp2.&colon. a pair of jacks or better is the lowest paying hand.
:li.:hp2.Bonus Deluxe:ehp2.&colon. like Jacks or Better, with a larger payout for four of a kind.
:li.:hp2.Deuces Wild:ehp2.&colon. all four deuces (twos) are wild and stand for any card; three of a kind is the lowest paying hand. The deuces are marked on the cards.
:eul.
:p.
Every game has its own payout table, shown above the cards.

:h1 res=004.Advice and odds
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
The :hp2.Advice:ehp2. button (key A) marks the cards to discard which give the highest expected payout for the present wager. The :hp2.Odds:ehp2. button (key O) shows the probability of each kind of hand for the cards you have marked, and the expected payout.
:p.
A good practice is to pick the cards yourself first, then use Advice to compare. In some hands several choices are equally good; the program shows only one. A game library without odds disables both buttons.

:h1 res=005.Menus and keys
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Game&colon. New Game (Ctrl+N) sets the bank to $25 between hands; Select chooses the game; Exit (Ctrl+X). Options&colon. Sound switches the sound effects; Language selects English, Spanish, Dutch, German, French or Italian, and menus, dialogs and this help change at once; Frame Controls (Ctrl+F) hides or shows the title bar and menu; Save settings on exit stores the settings, the bank and the last game in MPoker.cfg.
:p.
Keys&colon.
:dl tsize=18.
:dt.:hp2.F5 - F9, 1 - 5:ehp2.
:dd.Keep or discard card 1 to 5
:dt.:hp2.D:ehp2.
:dd.Deal
:dt.:hp2.+:ehp2.
:dd.Bet
:dt.:hp2.Space:ehp2.
:dd.Bet Five
:dt.:hp2.A:ehp2.
:dd.Advice
:dt.:hp2.O:ehp2.
:dd.Odds
:dt.:hp2.F1:ehp2.
:dd.Help
:edl.

:h1 res=006.About Multi Poker and license
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Multi Poker is part of The Compulsive Gambler's Toolkit by IglooSoft (1999), released as open source in 2002. The Open Watcom version was prepared by the OS2World community in 2026.
:p.
Multi Poker is free software&colon. you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License or (at your option) any later version. It is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY. See the file LICENSE.txt.

:euserdoc.
